  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "style": "large",
      "html": "<p>The Potomac runs 405 miles from the Allegheny Mountains to the Chesapeake Bay. Its last stretch above tidewater drops sharply over the fall line, and nearly everything about the region's history follows from that drop.</p>"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "html": "<h2>The fall line</h2><p>Scroll to follow the river downstream. The map on the right moves with the story.</p>"
    },
    {
      "type": "sidecar",
      "layout": "docked",
      "slides": [
        {
          "html": "<h3>Great Falls</h3><p>The river falls 76 feet in under a mile, through the narrow Mather Gorge. Boats could not get past it, so cargo had to stop here.</p>",
          "media": {
            "type": "map",
            "view": {
              "center": [
                -77.2539,
                38.9985
              ],
              "zoom": 14,
              "pitch": 45,
              "bearing": -20,
              "basemap": "streets",
              "markers": [
                {
                  "lngLat": [
                    -77.2539,
                    38.9985
                  ],
                  "title": "Great Falls",
                  "text": "Mather Gorge overlook"
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "html": "<h3>Georgetown</h3><p>A tobacco port grew up at the head of navigation, the farthest point upriver that seagoing ships could reach.</p>",
          "media": {
            "type": "map",
            "view": {
              "center": [
                -77.061,
                38.9025
              ],
              "zoom": 15,
              "pitch": 30,
              "bearing": 0,
              "basemap": "streets",
              "markers": [
                {
                  "lngLat": [
                    -77.061,
                    38.9025
                  ],
                  "title": "Georgetown Waterfront"
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "html": "<h3>An image slide</h3><p>A slide can show an image, video or embedded page instead of the map. The map comes back on the next slide.</p>",
          "media": {
            "type": "image",
            "url": "https://picsum.photos/seed/georgetown/1600/1000",
            "alt": "Placeholder photo"
          }
        },
        {
          "html": "<h3>The National Mall</h3><p>Much of the Mall and West Potomac Park sits on land dredged from the river's tidal flats in the 1880s. See the <a href=\"#action:parks\">federal park land</a> along the river, or zoom in on the <a href=\"#action:memorials\">memorials</a>.</p>",
          "media": {
            "type": "map",
            "view": {
              "center": [
                -77.045,
                38.885
              ],
              "zoom": 13.5,
              "pitch": 0,
              "bearing": 0,
              "basemap": "light",
              "markers": [
                {
                  "lngLat": [
                    -77.0502,
                    38.8893
                  ],
                  "title": "Lincoln Memorial"
                }
              ],
              "layers": [
                "landmarks"
              ]
            }
          },
          "actions": [
            {
