              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "html": "<h3>Old Town Alexandria</h3><p>Downstream, Alexandria's deep-water port competed with Georgetown for the river trade.</p>",
          "media": {
            "type": "map",
            "view": {
              "center": [
                -77.0393,
                38.8048
              ],
              "zoom": 14.5,
              "pitch": 40,
              "bearing": 15,
              "basemap": "streets",
              "markers": [
                {
                  "lngLat": [
                    -77.0393,
                    38.8048
                  ],
                  "title": "Alexandria waterfront"
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "html": "<h3>The whole route</h3><p>Zoomed out, the run from the falls to Mount Vernon is about 30 miles. The Mount Vernon Trail follows the Virginia shore for the last 18.</p>",
          "media": {
            "type": "map",
            "view": {
              "center": [
                -77.12,
                38.86
              ],
              "zoom": 10,
              "pitch": 0,
